{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Do not fear him.</b> And concerning Sihon there was no need to say 'do not fear him' — rather, Moses was afraid lest the merit of his having served Abraham not stand for him, as it is said (Genesis 14) ״וַיָּבֹא הַפָּלִיט״ — and that is Og."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:45.755295643Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}